{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mqe9hy58oqj","workspace":"/Users/imyu/Desktop/zonoid","title":"Cost data loss: usage records are overlay-local, not graph-durable","summary":"Billing data (usage_records, usage_reconcile_snapshot) lives only in the overlay JSON file (~/.claude/orchestrator/overlay/zonoid-*.json), not in the graph store. Two separate failure modes: (1) transcript pruning — reconcile() re-reads live .jsonl files in ~/.claude/projects/<ws>/; when Claude Code prunes old transcripts, those tokens vanish from billing permanently because snapshot.totals is REPLACED not accumulated (usage-reconcile.js:35); (2) overlay reset — daemon restart loses the usage_reconcile watermark, next reconcile starts from scratch against whatever transcripts survive. Fix requires: emitting usage_recorded graph events per task node (task_key slices → task node, no-key slices → system:billing node) and making reconcile accumulate into running totals (mergeTotals into prev snapshot) instead of replacing.","created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-06-14T20:53:51.260Z","vec":[-0.12557187676429749,0.06813640892505646,-0.035447292029857635,0.004012012388557196,0.013220231048762798,-0.05572447553277016,-0.06200708821415901,0.04413869231939316,0.026526574045419693,0.041410624980926514,0.002889117691665888,0.02627839893102646,0.006339068524539471,-0.007517700549215078,0.023323267698287964,-0.01852228119969368,-0.0394393689930439,-0.010481507517397404,-0.03962300345301628,-0.028281833976507187,-0.06141580641269684,0.0011966860620304942,-0.031096700578927994,0.04820183292031288,0.08523847907781601,0.04912249371409416,-0.08559734374284744,0.01816345565021038,0.023004775866866112,-0.013343438506126404,0.04256891831755638,0.05465429276227951,0.017472142353653908,-0.0059983497485518456,0.05384448170661926,0.09019619226455688,0.009037893265485764,-0.004679205361753702,0.02265571802854538,-0.028074288740754128,0.038601744920015335,0.06429911404848099,-0.11799225211143494,-0.006463431287556887,-0.0